  "interface_edits": [
    "Use endpoint(...) in the copied optical and mineral equation strings and the KdV trace calls; ntrace(p) becomes endpoint(p, deriv=1).",
    "Keep only the KdV numerical assembly, diagnostic, geometry and linear-solver helpers; resolve their imports locally.",
    "Keep scaling graph generators locally without campaign/partition-controller imports.",
    "Beam adds a finite-error assertion and a structured RESULT record.",
    "Steady rods use native grad/div, continuous regularity, automatic taus and a vertex constraint.",
    "New small entry points use bounded default inputs and numerical checks. They do not inherit historical paper-run qualification.",
    "Ordinary KdV now declares continuous u, grad/div and paired endpoint slope constraints. The new tau='adjoint' assembly generates physical-L2 constraint adjoints internally; serial small-case matrices, nonlinear projection, three steps and rates are compared with explicit_reference.py.",
    "Transient rods and scaling use dt/grad/div, continuous physical fields and native vertex constraints. Dedalus combines the shared vertex balance across the original heterogeneous resolution groups and generates edge taus internally.",
    "Carrier optics uses E@grad and endpoint selections/sums with automatic taus; the exact fixed-carrier physics and pencil are preserved. The direct physical-field optical helper also uses native grad/div.",
    "Mineral pressure uses a continuous field, distributional div and prescribed vertex constraints. Its Dirac source retains compensated pressure defect correction and cached geometry updates.",
    "Scaling writes the u and v equations explicitly within one loop over resolution groups. Coefficients, manufactured profiles, sampled cubes, coupling and original discretization remain visible in the script.",
    "Mineral transport uses only the exact uniform-pore integrating factor and fully mixed junctions, with no fitted flag or formulation branch. Direct concentration and optional custom mixing alternatives are retained in dedalus/tests/mineral_transport_verification.py.",
    "KdV selects tau='adjoint', constructing correction shapes from the physical-L2 adjoints of the junction conditions. The old 'galerkin' spelling remains an alias; the numerical implementation is unchanged."
  ],
